==German==

===Etymology===
From {{der|de|gmh|wandern}}, from {{der|de|goh|*wantarōn}}, from {{der|de|gmw-pro|*wandarōn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈvandɐn/}}
* {{hyphenation|de|wan|dern}}
* {{audio|de|De-wandern.ogg|a=Germany}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-wandern.ogg|a=Austria}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|<sein,haben[rare]>}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[hike]]
#: {{ux|de|Ich war im Wald '''wandern''', als ich das Reh sah.|I was '''hiking''' in the woods when I saw the deer.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[wander]], to [[migrate]], to move [[spontaneously]], to [[end up]] (somewhere)
#: {{ux|de|Lassen Sie Ihren Gedanken einfach '''wandern'''.|Just let your thoughts '''wander'''.}}
#: {{ux|de|Die Elektronen '''wandern''' zur Anode.|The electrons '''migrate''' to the anode.}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich fürchte, du wirst in den Knast '''wandern'''.|I'm afraid you'll '''end up''' in jail.}}

====Usage notes====
* The auxiliary is necessarily {{m|de||sein}} when a direction is given: {{m|de||Wir sind zum See gewandert.|t=We took a hike to the lake.}} Without a direction, both auxiliaries are possible, but {{m|de||sein}} is still vastly predominant: {{m|de||In diesen Bergen sind/haben wir oft gewandert.|t=We used to take frequent hikes in these mountains.}}

